    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d242-a1">

                <pb facs="0411" n="315" sameAs="frus:frus1872p1/pg315"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Marsh to Visconti Venosta.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States.</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Borne</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1871-12-27"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 27,
                        1871</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi> As the best method of complying with the
                    orders of my Government in relation to services rendered to the United States
                    ship of war Guerriere by officers of the Italian navy, I have the honor to
                    inclose you copies of a recent instruction on that subject from the Secretary of
                    State of the United States, and of a communication from the Secretary of the
                    Navy to the State Department.</p>
                <p>I avail myself of the occasion to renew to you the assurance of my high
                    consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>GEORGE P. MARSH.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>The Noble Chevalier <hi rendition="#small-caps">Visconti
                            Venosta</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Minister of Foreign
                            Affairs.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
